{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod","id":990992,"title":"Pre-Columbian WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T09:40:32-07:00","id":990992,"title":"Pre-Columbian WoD","content":"Perhaps there's some ideas of a Pre-Columbian WoD or rather a &quot;Dark Ages&quot; setting taking place in Pre-Columbian America?<br /> <br /> For example, due to the American continent being 'different' to Europe especially it's 'paradigm', maybe perhaps the supernaturals originally inhabited there are Wendigo and Utkena (Not the Werewolf tribes but the real ones from folklore), Kachinas, etc?<br /> <br /> Also perhaps in Mesoamerican society, maybe perhaps their creation stories (human made from maize) and their Deities are also are all real and true which for example, Huitzilopochtli is exactly what he is, a deity not a Baali Methuselah which could be lies made up by the Sabbat vampires who invaded there (matter of fact, I'm not a big fan of &quot;Kindred impersonating as Deities&quot; thing which is rather problematic and I think it's best to present them being lies made up by Christian vampires as a attempt to demonize other Deities that is not Yahweh, meaning that Odin, Ishtar, Kali, etc are actually Deities not Vampires).<br /> <br /> Of course the only closest reference to Pre-Columbian Vampires is the tale of <a href=\"https://authorlyngibson.wordpress.com/2014/05/01/the-jumlin-a-vampire-legend-from-the-cherokee-nation/\" target=\"_blank\">Jumlin</a> which their description is entirely different to the Kindred's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 10-21-2016, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T11:40:11-07:00","id":991050,"title":"","content":"There's Croatan Song, and that's about it. Being a Werewolf book, it gives no shits about paradigms or &quot;thaumivory&quot;, and just has an array of unaccountable beings in its antagonist section that exist regardless of whether you believe in them or not. Presumably, many of them would still be around in the modern day.<br /> <br /> (Also, even if Odin isn't actually a vampire, he'd still be an asshole. FENRIS FOREVER! STRIKE DOWN THE AESIR!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T11:55:40-07:00","id":991055,"title":"","content":"There are actually plenty of pre-Columbian 'vampires'. The Civitateo of Central America and the Pishtaco of South America are both vampires, though it could be argued that they are closer to the Kuei-jin than the Kindred (depending on your point of view).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:09:51-07:00","id":991058,"title":"","content":"The pre-Columbian Americas is where the Mage worldview has trouble. Mage says that consensus shapes reality. In a Euro-centric view, they've explained how that would result in a world largely like the real world at most points in history. In the Americas, it would be a big divergence.<br /> <br /> For example - the Order of Reason had to slowly build firearms into the consensus in Europe. Sorcerer's Crusade covers a time when very basic firearms were in the consensus and could be used by anyone, but more reliable/powerful ones were not - so they only show up in that setting as a focus for a High Artisan to work his Enlightened Will with, or as a Wonder/Device imbued with its own ability to warp reality. If that's true, when Europeans landed in America and tried to use their firearms, shouldn't they have been Paradoxical again? Nobody in the Americas, aside from the other guys on the ship, believed in them, so they should have only worked for Enlightened folks who could warp reality.<br /> <br /> If the Europeans land and their guns don't work, then no conquering is really going to happen, and we diverge from real-world history too much. You'll have to come up with a reason why technology accepted by Europeans but not by Americans worked in America. For the guns example:<ul><li>There weren't a lot of guns on the landing ships - mostly swords and other simpler things. The guns they did have were actually operated by High Artisans or were Devices donated to the expedition by supportive Artisans back home.</li> <li>The guns they used were much crappier than in the real world - arquebuses, hand-cannons, etc. Those were barely consensual enough to not explode most of the time, but still allowed them to take over natives via shock and awe.</li> <li>They didn't bring guns at all, and conquered native cultures not with technology but by pitting them against each other and spreading disease.</li> </ul>For the spiritual landscape - yes, I think having a generally lower Gauntlet in the Americas and a more common spiritual presence makes sense. Note that the Uktena took it as their job to find all the bad Banes and bind them, so aside from these areas of binding, the spiritual landscape should be in pretty good shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","user":"haldir2012","date":". 10-21-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:28:24-07:00","id":991062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991058#post991058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pre-Columbian Americas is where the Mage worldview has trouble. Mage says that consensus shapes reality. In a Euro-centric view, they've explained how that would result in a world largely like the real world at most points in history. In the Americas, it would be a big divergence.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I've guessed from what I've read of Mage: The Ascension is that one of the reasons that people in WoD seem to have the same history as in real life is because half of what New World Order does is historical revision. If you want to champion modern medicine over faith healings, potions etc., say that before modern medicine, everyone died from disgusting diseases before they turned 30. So originally, maybe guns <i>didn't</i> play a big part in the conquest of the Americas, but history <i>says</i> otherwise. I imagine that the modern consensus might be able to truly change the past, although I don't know if it works like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:46:48-07:00","id":991073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991058#post991058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pre-Columbian Americas is where the Mage worldview has trouble. Mage says that consensus shapes reality. In a Euro-centric view, they've explained how that would result in a world largely like the real world at most points in history. In the Americas, it would be a big divergence.<br /> <br /> For example - the Order of Reason had to slowly build firearms into the consensus in Europe. Sorcerer's Crusade covers a time when very basic firearms were in the consensus and could be used by anyone, but more reliable/powerful ones were not - so they only show up in that setting as a focus for a High Artisan to work his Enlightened Will with, or as a Wonder/Device imbued with its own ability to warp reality. If that's true, when Europeans landed in America and tried to use their firearms, shouldn't they have been Paradoxical again? Nobody in the Americas, aside from the other guys on the ship, believed in them, so they should have only worked for Enlightened folks who could warp reality.<br /> <br /> If the Europeans land and their guns don't work, then no conquering is really going to happen, and we diverge from real-world history too much. You'll have to come up with a reason why technology accepted by Europeans but not by Americans worked in America. For the guns example:<ul><li>There weren't a lot of guns on the landing ships - mostly swords and other simpler things. The guns they did have were actually operated by High Artisans or were Devices donated to the expedition by supportive Artisans back home.</li> <li>The guns they used were much crappier than in the real world - arquebuses, hand-cannons, etc. Those were barely consensual enough to not explode most of the time, but still allowed them to take over natives via shock and awe.</li> <li>They didn't bring guns at all, and conquered native cultures not with technology but by pitting them against each other and spreading disease.</li> </ul><br /> For the spiritual landscape - yes, I think having a generally lower Gauntlet in the Americas and a more common spiritual presence makes sense. Note that the Uktena took it as their job to find all the bad Banes and bind them, so aside from these areas of binding, the spiritual landscape should be in pretty good shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the biggest problem with Mage's worldview (along with Ars Magica that it's based on) that it takes on a Eurocentric basis which is pretty problematic which is why I think it needs to be revised or rewritten to be less so to be more diverse especially taking in a &quot;All Myths are True&quot; angle which is perhaps how the world was before the current consensus took over everything.<br /> <br /> One idea that before the consensus, all of reality was the tellueran (which meant the physical world and the umbra being the low/middle/high/deep/etc were all one) which means all reality were endless fluid pocket realms before the Order of Reason solidified everything into a planet we see today.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991062#post991062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I've guessed from what I've read of Mage: The Ascension is that one of the reasons that people in WoD seem to have the same history as in real life is because half of what New World Order does is historical revision. If you want to champion modern medicine over faith healings, potions etc., say that before modern medicine, everyone died from disgusting diseases before they turned 30. So originally, maybe guns <i>didn't</i> play a big part in the conquest of the Americas, but history <i>says</i> otherwise. I imagine that the modern consensus might be able to truly change the past, although I don't know if it works like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the other idea being simply that the Order of Reason's paradigm (the Spanish Conquistadors, Columbus, etc) simply conflicted and &quot;overridden&quot; the Mesoamerican's with force via imperialism (hence why their guns worked) which basically &quot;overthrew it&quot; and replaced it with their own hence the atrocities committed especially the Spanish burning all or most of the their books as a attempt to override their paradigm with theirs instead of peacefully synchronizing it much like Ancient societies did in the past ala <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greco-Buddhism\" target=\"_blank\">Greco-buddhism</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 10-21-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:26:47-07:00","id":991085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991058#post991058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the spiritual landscape - yes, I think having a generally lower Gauntlet in the Americas and a more common spiritual presence makes sense. Note that the Uktena took it as their job to find all the bad Banes and bind them, so aside from these areas of binding, the spiritual landscape should be in pretty good shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except in the cities that the First Nations folk built, anyway. Croatan Song put any notion of actual &quot;Pure&quot; Lands to bed rather harshly, as a not at all insignificant amount of the Croatan's kin were lost to corruption, and they had to raze some cities where their kin were living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:33:50-07:00","id":991120,"title":"","content":"The big difficulty with Pre-Columbian America as a setting is that before there was time to understand it it had all but been destroyed. We are ferociously ignorant of how life actually worked, especially on the larger scale. It's something that historians are busy revising and learning to this day. A recent study I read suggests that the population of the Americas before Europeans arrived was 70,000,000 with vibrant inter-cultural exchange and more languages and traditions than we can differentiate. Partially due to war and enslavement, though mostly due to diseases like influenze and smallpox, a century later the population of the Americas was less than 4,000,000. Two continents of humans almost totally collapsed. So much was lost that we can never truly get back that you'd have to be very careful and thorough with your research and still acknowledge you were likely to be wrong about 1001 things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-21-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T18:49:29-07:00","id":991211,"title":"","content":"That is true. It was not until two decades ago that we understood that there was a pre-Columbian Amazonian civilization that may have possessed a population of nearly 20 million human beings due to the fertility of the Indian Black Earth (which represents the largest manmade structure ever). The total population of the Americas was probably closer to 100 million human beings, one fifth of the population of the Earth, but the vast majority of their cultures and their languages were lost due to the genocide that they experienced. I would suggest that there is no culture that would be impossible, considering that we have the extremes that range from the Lenape (matriarchal mystic diplomat farmers) to the Aztecs (patriarchal cannibalistic merchant warriors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T05:12:39-07:00","id":991346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod#post990992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also perhaps in Mesoamerican society, maybe perhaps their creation stories (human made from maize) and their Deities are also are all real and true which for example, Huitzilopochtli is exactly what he is, a deity not a Baali Methuselah which could be lies made up by the Sabbat vampires who invaded there (matter of fact, I'm not a big fan of &quot;Kindred impersonating as Deities&quot; thing which is rather problematic and I think it's best to present them being lies made up by Christian vampires as a attempt to demonize other Deities that is not Yahweh, meaning that Odin, Ishtar, Kali, etc are actually Deities not Vampires).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's Tlaloc. Tlaloc is an Aztec Deity that:<br /> <br /> 1- Is not a Cainite.<br /> 2- Has nothing to do with Caine myth or anything on those lines.<br /> 3- Nobody lied about its identity.<br /> 4- Is worshiped by Sabbat Koldun and Aztec vampires.<br /> 5- Really, WW is White Wolf, not White Washing.<br /> <br /> It's just Huitzilopochtli that happened to be Shaitan. And as far as Camarilla/Sabbat are concerned, neither of them has any interest in lying about its identity. Especially when the first Sabbat to reach the lands were loyalists that are till today heavily influenced by native American culture (as proved by their ritae and the considerable number of native Gangrel/Ravnos).<br /> They would probably have believed Huitzilopochtli to be a native God, but the surge of Infernalists and the Black Hand's Investigations pointed at it being a false God and a Methuselah.<br /> <br /> And, Shaitan is not the only one using that kind of trick. There's an American entity that masqueraded as the eastern Archon Jaldabaoth that was worshiped by Sabbat Cathari (your &quot;christian&quot; vampires) before they've been slaughtered by the Inquisition. So...really, it's not just &quot;christians&quot; that pull out those tricks.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh and...really, nobody knows if Yahweh is the Yahweh that we think it is. For all we know, it could be another usurper God or even the Archon itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 10-22-2016, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T08:44:58-07:00","id":991406,"title":"","content":"Or anything at all. Archeological evidence suggests that the original Yahweh was a volcano diety of the Sinai peninsula who was worshipped by the ancient people of that region as part of an extended pantheon. El, King of Gods, and his three wives were the primary deities until Yahweh replaced El as the chief of the gods around the 9th century BC, which represented the first theological split of the Hebrews with the other people of Canaan. By the end of the Babylonian exile, the other gods had been abandoned due to the influence of Zorastranism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T09:12:40-07:00","id":991412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991346#post991346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there's Tlaloc. Tlaloc is an Aztec Deity that:<br /> <br /> 1- Is not a Cainite.<br /> 2- Has nothing to do with Caine myth or anything on those lines.<br /> 3- Nobody lied about its identity.<br /> 4- Is worshiped by Sabbat Koldun and Aztec vampires.<br /> 5- Really, WW is White Wolf, not White Washing.<br /> <br /> It's just Huitzilopochtli that happened to be Shaitan. And as far as Camarilla/Sabbat are concerned, neither of them has any interest in lying about its identity. Especially when the first Sabbat to reach the lands were loyalists that are till today heavily influenced by native American culture (as proved by their ritae and the considerable number of native Gangrel/Ravnos).<br /> <b>They would probably have believed Huitzilopochtli to be a native God, but the surge of Infernalists and the Black Hand's Investigations pointed at it being a false God and a Methuselah.</b><br /> <br /> And, Shaitan is not the only one using that kind of trick. There's an American entity that masqueraded as the eastern Archon Jaldabaoth that was worshiped by Sabbat Cathari (your &quot;christian&quot; vampires) before they've been slaughtered by the Inquisition. So...really, it's not just &quot;christians&quot; that pull out those tricks.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's exactly where I was trying to point out how <i>problematic</i> the WoD canon actually is since this is a pure example of cultural appropriation which it's apart of a very problematic trope that beings (whether being vampires, demons, etc) posing as gods and are treated as the &quot;Source of the Myths&quot; which is the result of where white writers simply approached a culture that does not belong to them and used it as their plaything but meanwhile....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991346#post991346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Oh and...really, nobody knows if Yahweh is the Yahweh that we think it is. For all we know, it could be another usurper God or even the Archon itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet WoD lore makes it very clear that the Yahweh we think of IS the actual Yahweh because he's allowed to be treated as a real deity (although he actually was a usurper Deity on EL though) yet the other deities are labeled &quot;False Gods&quot; which is downright offensive.<br /> <br /> Then again above all else, this is why using Abrahamic mythoes as a basis sends a very dangerous message because it runs a huge risk of &quot;White people are right therefore imperialism is totally justified&quot; and has racism embedded in it's core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 10-22-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T09:37:38-07:00","id":991417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991412#post991412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's exactly where I was trying to point out how <i>problematic</i> the WoD canon actually is since this is a pure example of cultural appropriation which it's apart of a very problematic trope that beings (whether being vampires, demons, etc) posing as gods and are treated as the &quot;Source of the Myths&quot; which is the result of where white writers simply approached a culture that does not belong to them and used it as their plaything but meanwhile....</div> </div> </div> </div>You've used the word &quot;problematic&quot; more times in one week than I did in 20 years...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then again above all else, this is why using Abrahamic mythoes as a basis sends a very dangerous message because it runs a huge risk of &quot;White people are right therefore imperialism is totally justified&quot; and has racism embedded in it's core. </div> </div> </div>So, it's like I said last time. You're not here to discuss the game, you're just here to militate against WW's portrayal of WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 10-22-2016, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T09:46:10-07:00","id":991418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991406#post991406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or anything at all. Archeological evidence suggests that the original Yahweh was a volcano diety of the Sinai peninsula who was worshipped by the ancient people of that region as part of an extended pantheon. El, King of Gods, and his three wives were the primary deities until Yahweh replaced El as the chief of the gods around the 9th century BC, which represented the first theological split of the Hebrews with the other people of Canaan. By the end of the Babylonian exile, the other gods had been abandoned due to the influence of Zorastranism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like to see some sources to back that up, because it doesn't really match up with anything I've ever seen. It ignores Baal, both in the singular and plural sense, utterly, and pretty much all archaeological evidence points to the importance of Ba'al in pretty much every way, everywhere the Canaaites went. Including the Phoencian era expansion across the Mediterranean where they established nearly complete hegemony across North Africa and up into the Iberian peninsula. Textual sources, both Hebrew and otherwise, indicate the importance of Ba'al, as well. There are even depictions of the two together in artistic formats by Hebrew and other Canaanites, where Ba'al and Yahweh are depicted together, with Ba'al always depicted as the higher status deity (and, incidentally with some female deity indicated to be at the same &quot;level&quot; as Yahweh and subordinate to Ba'al). Not to diminish the importance of Asherah, Astarte &amp; Anat (no matter how you slice those three/two/one, oh yeah, and Tanit....), but to put them at the top of the pile doesn't seem to be backed up by the majority of the evidence. Co-equal, maybe, but not at the top. And even then, it's Ba'al who is the King. It's El who can give away kingship/the right to have a palace. Anat and Astarte may have a lot to do with Ba'al becoming king (including beating the crap out of El for dithering), but it's not she who rules.<br /> <br /> And Yahweh doesn't seem to be much of a volcano god. There aren't any volcanoes in the relevant area, for one. He also seems to be associated with atmospheric phenomena, which is one of the reasons for the syncretization with El (and, sometimes, much to the chagrin of the Hebrew priestly caste, with Ba'al as well). He MIGHT have some sea/dragon aspects and have something to do with Yam.... but that is really weak, especially since some of the oldest Yahweh stories depict him as a dragon fighter (which is probably borrowed from Ba'al battling with various dragon-ish things, including Yam and with syncretization with Marduk during the Babylonian exile).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T09:46:35-07:00","id":991419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991417#post991417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it's like I said last time. You're not here to discuss the game, you're just here to militate against WW's portrayal of WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still discussing the game but while pointing out things that I'm rather critical in some aspects while I'm trying to look for changes to fix up a few things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:07:24-07:00","id":991427,"title":"","content":"As has been pointed out, pre-Columbian is going to be a hard row to hoe, especially if you are looking at North America. At best, what exists in European records is recording either, effectively, a post-Apocalyptic or peri-Apocalyptic time. There isn't much to indicate what was going on before Europeans showed up anywhere in North America, except, pehaps if you want to read (wade) through De Vega's book on the Entrada of Hernando de Soto, and even that covers a small section of the continent (Western Florida along the Gulf Coast through Georgia, Alabama &amp; Mississippi and up into Arkansas before it all went south). Maybe a decent chance of getting something sold out of the Southwest and maybe the Northwest coast. But, overall, it's going to take a fair amount of hardcore scholarship for any particular area. Unless you want to make it up pretty much whole cloth. And that's assuming by Pre-Columbian, you mean &quot;right before Columbus&quot;. If you are talking about prior to that (since Pre-Columbian technically extends back to Clovis folks running around killing mammoths and further), it's going to get even more difficult. as you are going to be slogging through archaeological monographs. <br /> <br /> Things are slightly different if you are thinking about Central America or Eastern South America, things are bit easier...<br /> <br /> I don't think the major issue with the Technocratic/Mage issue with the conquest of the Americas is the possession and operations of guns. It's how and why disease was the issue. Since that's THE issue. Guns were all well and good, but, they're guns of that era. They are kinda cool, but they are slow and somewhat dangerous. An army of Aztecs could easily have thrown enough bodies at Cortez to remove any advantage received by his guns (and metal armor and horses and metal swords). Cortez was able to do what he did because he moved fast, he was super-duper strange (an &quot;out of context&quot; event), he sure as hell seemed like he fit right into their mythology as a &quot;good guy&quot;, the subjects of the Aztecs HATED them and were more than willing to lend their assistance, and, oh yeah, the Aztecs were super-duper sick because the European diseases were moving faster than Cortez, including their leader. (The messengers taking the news about the conquistadors' arrival were transmitting the disease as they raced to the capital). It was pretty much the same with Pizzaro, et al.<br /> <br /> In fact, in some ways that argues FOR the ideas of Mage. A very small group of guys could easily be mages and that era's version of &quot;extraordinary&quot; citizens. After all, if the Void Explorers could manage to keep a whole ship &quot;in paradigm&quot; so that it could even go to places with different types of belief, they could probably keep small mobile groups equivalently supported. Sure the guns worked. Because the gun mages were there and all of the guys with them sure believed in guns. So the funs worked. Then you take into account you are killing off most of the folks with the different belief structure, subverting that same belief structure and imposing a top down governmental group-think, the Pre-Columbian paradigms shatter pretty effectively, pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> A major concern would seem to be what the Hell, the Tradition and non-Tradition mages native to the Americas were doing while all this was going on... I.e. Why did the Order of Reason get away with it seemingly largely unopposed. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:24:33-07:00","id":991479,"title":"","content":"There are several active volcanoes in Syria (Al-Safa erupted in 1850 AD). The Dead Sea is a rift valley, and it is bordered by dozens of dormant volcanoes, some of whom erupted within the last ten thousand years. There are also active volcanoes throughout the Rea Sea region, so the ancient peoples of Canaan were quite familiar with volcanoes. In addition, there is a 40,000 square kilometer volcanic field, Harrat al-Shamah, which contains 800 volcanic cones and possessed a lake of lava as recently as the 19th century.<br /> <br /> Ba'al is a title, similar to El, and it just means 'my lord'. Ba'al was the name given by the Phoenicians while El was the name given by the Hebrews (because of the nature and similarity of two written languages, it is more properly b'l verses 'l, which may be as simple as the difference between 'my lord' and 'lord', meaning that Ba'al and El may be the exactly same entity). The superiority of Ba'al/El over Yahweh would have been quite appropriate, given the historical inferiority of Yahweh to Ba'al/El within the pantheon of Canaan. Initially, Yahweh may have been a hero god, similar to Hercules or Thor, who was elevated to supremacy as his hero cult became more and more popular among the Hebrews.<br /> <br /> There is also evidence that Ba'al/El may have been derived from the Egyptian deity Ptah, the god of craftsman, which would have also been the god of carpenters. That would lead to an interesting idea that Jesus, who was a carpenter, may have been the son of Ba'al/El (Ptah) instead of the son of Yahweh, which would have fit nicely within the thousands of years of Egyptian influence of the region (even during the rule of the Romans). Of course, this is all conjecture because the majority of the texts in the region were burned first by the Christians during the first century AD and then the Muslims during the 7th century AD, so we really do not have much of an idea of how the ancient religions of the region interrelated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 10-22-2016, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T19:44:17-07:00","id":991664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991479#post991479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ba'al is a title, similar to El, and it just means 'my lord'. Ba'al was the name given by the Phoenicians while El was the name given by the Hebrews (because of the nature and similarity of two written languages, it is more properly b'l verses 'l, which may be as simple as the difference between 'my lord' and 'lord', meaning that Ba'al and El may be the exactly same entity). The superiority of Ba'al/El over Yahweh would have been quite appropriate, given the historical inferiority of Yahweh to Ba'al/El within the pantheon of Canaan. Initially, Yahweh may have been a hero god, similar to Hercules or Thor, who was elevated to supremacy as his hero cult became more and more popular among the Hebrews.<br /> <br /> There is also evidence that Ba'al/El may have been derived from the Egyptian deity Ptah, the god of craftsman, which would have also been the god of carpenters. That would lead to an interesting idea that Jesus, who was a carpenter, may have been the son of Ba'al/El (Ptah) instead of the son of Yahweh, which would have fit nicely within the thousands of years of Egyptian influence of the region (even during the rule of the Romans). Of course, this is all conjecture because the majority of the texts in the region were burned first by the Christians during the first century AD and then the Muslims during the 7th century AD, so we really do not have much of an idea of how the ancient religions of the region interrelated.</div> </div> </div> </div>In any case, Yahweh isn't and never has been associated with volcanoes. Mountains. Yes. Well... more accurately &quot;high places&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ba'al is a title. &quot;Lord/King of&quot; But it's also nominative. Ba'al &quot;X&quot; can mean &quot;Lord/King/God of X&quot; but, mythologically, Ba'al is also one guy, properly Ba'al Haddad. Even though there are &quot;different&quot; Ba'al's of different cities, that doesn't mean they aren't also Ba'al Haddad. Meaning, there is a mythological figure with associated myths that was identified as Ba'al, That's the guy who all the Hebrew priests are pissed off that the Israeli's are worshping. As in, that is the name written on the statue or next to the depiction. So... yeah. It is a title, but, that doesn't meant it's not a name or specific personage.<br /> <br /> Ba'al is not El. El, who is not Yahweh. More the reverse. Yahweh was syncretized to the much older El, who is a different figure with his own myths and attributions. (Like adding on all the Marduk stuff as well. Like shedding the wives et al. as henotheism gave way to monolatrism) Old Heliocentric attributions to Ptah don't hold. Sure, there might be some Egyptians looking for a &quot;match&quot; when talking about the gods of the Canaanites, but that doesn't make such an attribution real for most purposes. (It can of course have been real, in that an Egyptian might have left an offering to Ptah in a temple of El and felt that the two were one.... but that's on the Egyptian. It doesn't make El into Ptah.) That's like saying that Taranis is really Mars, just because that's what the Romans called him when they were dedicating offerings to the local deities. Egyptians had hegemony over the region for a limited period of time (as did many many other groups), but much of the salient material predates Egyptian conquest. So that's like saying that the American domination of New York state clearly demonstrates that Hiawatha is, in fact, Thomas Jefferson.<br /> <br /> And neither Ba'al nor El are craftsman. There is a Canaanite god for that who both El and Ba'al have to call on when they want stuff made.... Kothar or Kothar-na-Hawis. He's an all around maker of stuff, from magical godly palaces to all powerful bows to magical clubs for Behemoth and Leviathan and death god smiting.<br /> <br /> None of this requires anything in the way of texts that the Christians might or might not have burned. These from contemporaneous documents of which we have LOTS. Many from the cultures in question and others from their neighbors. In addition to massive excavations of temples and other sites, graffiti, etc. etc. If there's any group of people who are destroying them, it's much more modern, as in ISIS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:19:15-07:00","id":991746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElizabethSterling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991120#post991120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big difficulty with Pre-Columbian America as a setting is that before there was time to understand it it had all but been destroyed. We are ferociously ignorant of how life actually worked, especially on the larger scale. It's something that historians are busy revising and learning to this day. A recent study I read suggests that the population of the Americas before Europeans arrived was 70,000,000 with vibrant inter-cultural exchange and more languages and traditions than we can differentiate. Partially due to war and enslavement, though mostly due to diseases like influenze and smallpox, a century later the population of the Americas was less than 4,000,000. Two continents of humans almost totally collapsed. So much was lost that we can never truly get back that you'd have to be very careful and thorough with your research and still acknowledge you were likely to be wrong about 1001 things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading that they estimate around 90% of the Native Americans died from diseases spread through the extensive trade routes that existed between the communities.. By the time Europeans began seriously exploring the central and mid-western parts of North America, for example, the native populations had undergone an extinction-level event a century or two earlier and so many of the habits, customs and civilizations that the explorers encountered weren't ones that had actually existed back in the 1500's, or at least were extremely different form the ones that had existed a century or two prior.<br /> <br /> This in turn means that descriptions of the people at the time don't necessarily give us entirely accurate insight into what life was actually like for the populations of the Americas prior to the arrival of Europeans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-23-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:29:43-07:00","id":991876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991746#post991746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember reading that they estimate around 90% of the Native Americans died from diseases spread through the extensive trade routes that existed between the communities.. By the time Europeans began seriously exploring the central and mid-western parts of North America, for example, the native populations had undergone an extinction-level event a century or two earlier and so many of the habits, customs and civilizations that the explorers encountered weren't ones that had actually existed back in the 1500's, or at least were extremely different form the ones that had existed a century or two prior.<br /> <br /> This in turn means that descriptions of the people at the time don't necessarily give us entirely accurate insight into what life was actually like for the populations of the Americas prior to the arrival of Europeans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. In addition, European innovations/imports were transmitted well in advance of actual contact. Such as the image of Plains tribes on horseback. There weren't any horses before the Spaniards brought them north of the desert between Aztec territory and the American Southwest. You don't need to learn much to take care of horses, compared, say, to developing the technological base required to make firearms. Those tribes were VERY different than they are typically depicted. They were agriculturalists who had some limited exploitation of the buffalo (actualy American bison, but whatever...), not nomadic hunters whose life centered around buffalo hunting. Etc. And the Pre-Contact lifeways were already generations gone by the time those tribes began meaningful contact with Europeans. <br /> <br /> This is very much the case in the North American Southeast as well. There was very complex culture there than was barely anything like that of the tribes met by later European expansion. Small cities with structured elites who lived above the populace on raised mounds that harken back more to a cultural continuity with antecedents from several centuries before that extended across vast swathes of the continent. Pretty much nothing like what was later there with Cherokee and their neighbors. <br /> <br /> Some very recent studies of the genetics of Pre-Contact remains vs. the genes of the remaining Native American populations indicates at least 90% of the genetic variability of the entire population was lost. Though the number of those who died is really almost impossible to determine for several factors (there are problems of chronology, trying to determine the original number, etc.) that is a population bottleneck that is nearly an extinction level event on the biological level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:35:19-07:00","id":991990,"title":"","content":"The Wraith Player's Guide and Shadow Player's Guide provide a little more information, specifically on the Flayed Lands, the Mesoamerican Dark Kingdom, and the metaphysics of its wraiths. As far as the Shadow Player's Guide is concerned, Quetzalcoatl and Tezcatlipoca are real - in the sense they're not guises for other entities - and Tezcatlipoca in particular manipulated Mesoamerican history to serve his own ends, gaining freedom from his ordained role in the cosmos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:35:44-07:00","id":992067,"title":"","content":"I'm sure Shattered Dreams when it comes will also be covering this stuff as well (given it covers such a huge time span in various lands).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:58:12-07:00","id":993336,"title":"","content":"Anyway there could be potential playable Vampires from Mesoamerica being the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tlahuelpuchi\" target=\"_blank\">Tlahuelpuchi</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cihuateteo\" target=\"_blank\">Civatateo</a> for example especially I'm looking for a way to create a Female Native American old western gunslinger drifter/outlaw vampire type character who is from Mexica or Pueblo or even Apache tradition (since I have taken a recent interest of Mexica and Pueblo culture at the moment but the same time I have to approach it carefully without appropriating it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 10-26-2016, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T01:07:35-07:00","id":993371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=991058#post991058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pre-Columbian Americas is where the Mage worldview has trouble. Mage says that consensus shapes reality. In a Euro-centric view, they've explained how that would result in a world largely like the real world at most points in history. In the Americas, it would be a big divergence.<br /> <br /> For example - the Order of Reason had to slowly build firearms into the consensus in Europe. Sorcerer's Crusade covers a time when very basic firearms were in the consensus and could be used by anyone, but more reliable/powerful ones were not - so they only show up in that setting as a focus for a High Artisan to work his Enlightened Will with, or as a Wonder/Device imbued with its own ability to warp reality. If that's true, when Europeans landed in America and tried to use their firearms, shouldn't they have been Paradoxical again? Nobody in the Americas, aside from the other guys on the ship, believed in them, so they should have only worked for Enlightened folks who could warp reality.<br /> <br /> If the Europeans land and their guns don't work, then no conquering is really going to happen, and we diverge from real-world history too much. You'll have to come up with a reason why technology accepted by Europeans but not by Americans worked in America. For the guns example:<ul><li>There weren't a lot of guns on the landing ships - mostly swords and other simpler things. The guns they did have were actually operated by High Artisans or were Devices donated to the expedition by supportive Artisans back home.</li> <li>The guns they used were much crappier than in the real world - arquebuses, hand-cannons, etc. Those were barely consensual enough to not explode most of the time, but still allowed them to take over natives via shock and awe.</li> <li>They didn't bring guns at all, and conquered native cultures not with technology but by pitting them against each other and spreading disease.</li> </ul>For the spiritual landscape - yes, I think having a generally lower Gauntlet in the Americas and a more common spiritual presence makes sense. Note that the Uktena took it as their job to find all the bad Banes and bind them, so aside from these areas of binding, the spiritual landscape should be in pretty good shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, guns didn't really have anything to do with it. Virulent continent wide pandemics of Measles, Small Pox and Plague turned the Americas into a post apocalyptic wasteland within a generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T06:41:54-07:00","id":994012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=993371#post993371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, guns didn't really have anything to do with it. Virulent continent wide pandemics of Measles, Small Pox and Plague turned the Americas into a post apocalyptic wasteland within a generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, like Ajax made above. <br /> <br /> It actually gives me a really evil idea. A group of Void Seekers charter their New World expedition, calling in favors with the Artificers and Craftmasons to get all kinds of goodies. They get there and are prepared to stick a flag in the ground and put it on a map, and damn the savages with my Titan's Armor and five-barreled repeating rifle. But suddenly, they find all the natives falling ill and dying. They come back and find that a Fallen Cosian archmage custom-built a Life effect to kill the populace of the New World, because what use is it if it's full of all those annoying people? Plus the Resonance will be <i>perfect</i>. The effect was built into something the expedition carried, and activated when they landed. Sure, the shamans of that land might save a few of their people, but the hard work is done. <br /> <br /> You're welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T10:47:55-07:00","id":994104,"title":"","content":"The problem with any genocidal magical effect is that there would have beens hundreds of Native American Mages and tens of thousands of Native American Sorcerers. Mundane disease is much more likely, especially if European Mages and Sorcerers are keeping their Native American peers busy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:44:18-07:00","id":998241,"title":"","content":"I think I just remembered what my original purpose of this thread was.<br /> <br /> Basically what I was proposing is a pure Pre-Columbian setting with all the folklore/mythologies and metaphysics intact without any Eurasian influence which means that it's essentially the &quot;Dark Ages&quot; setting set in Pre-Columbia America with all the Native nations (including Mesoamerican) intact or rather how Pre-Columbian life was like before Europeans which also means all their creation stories, deities, supernatural beings/creatures, etc are also all true and they're used to build the ground up.<br /> <br /> Or basically if there's any Pre-Columbian vampire or immortal equivalent especially existing in the West Coast or Mesoamerica, I think they could easily be translated in a Wild West game when Europeans eventually do show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:16:26-07:00","id":998749,"title":"","content":"Firearms in zones unfriendly to them can be explained as Order of Reason - or other Mages - being present and maintaing them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=994104#post994104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with any genocidal magical effect is that there would have beens hundreds of Native American Mages and tens of thousands of Native American Sorcerers. Mundane disease is much more likely, especially if European Mages and Sorcerers are keeping their Native American peers busy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence the need for a Cosian Archmage/Archmaster! Considering how strategically important neutralizing and taking over the Americas was, the creators of the Order of Reason could have even prepared the disease as a cabal.<br /> Alternatively, a Cosian could have made a whole expeditions into carriers of a mundane disease - or several diseases. Though you could argue that doing this is effectively a Magickal effect, and thus counterable by the native magicians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:13:49-07:00","id":998770,"title":"","content":"And there were no Native American Archmages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:35:10-07:00","id":998814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=998241#post998241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I just remembered what my original purpose of this thread was.<br /> <br /> Basically what I was proposing is a pure Pre-Columbian setting with all the folklore/mythologies and metaphysics intact without any Eurasian influence which means that it's essentially the &quot;Dark Ages&quot; setting set in Pre-Columbia America with all the Native nations (including Mesoamerican) intact or rather how Pre-Columbian life was like before Europeans which also means all their creation stories, deities, supernatural beings/creatures, etc are also all true and they're used to build the ground up.<br /> <br /> Or basically if there's any Pre-Columbian vampire or immortal equivalent especially existing in the West Coast or Mesoamerica, I think they could easily be translated in a Wild West game when Europeans eventually do show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still doesn't help a whole bunch.<br /> <br /> For many areas, the Pre-Columbian lifeways are nothing at all like what Europeans eventually saw. So, are you going to have Plains tribes that hunt bison from horseback? That's iconic Native American, but it wasn't anything like what was actually going on there. There were about as many horses on the Great Plains in Pre-Columbian times as there were Winchester rifles and Model T cars. The American Southeast was pretty much completely different than it was by the time of English contact. The area was dominated by the Southeastern Ceremonial Cult complex related cultures, which were a whole lot more like the much older Mississippian culture that came before them than they were like the Cherokee et al. that succeeded them. Much of what people &quot;know&quot; about Native American culture is actually seeing societies that are effectively Post-Apocalyptic So.... how much authenticity do you care about? It's going to seem off to the perceptions of most to delete the whole &quot;buffalo hunting horse riding Plains Indians&quot; and so on. So, do you chuck reality in favor of preconceived notions (which are often stereotypical to a great degree). <br /> <br /> In addition, you've said that the all the folklore/mythologies (and oh dear, opening that Pandora's jar is definitely a BIG thing) are intact and true, are you going to insert/overlay/shoehorn in the Eurocentric WoD stable of supernaturals? In an &quot;intact&quot; Pre-Columbian Mesoamerica, why are the gods vampires? In a pre-Cherokee North American Southeast, is Ulunsuti a Nosferatu? (If there even should be an Ulunsuti pre-Cherokee...) Why? She may have liked to stick her long fingernail in the livers of sleeping victims to get yummy treats but there's nothing to indicate that she had any problems with sunlight or need for blood. If you want the mythology intact, you are facing a situation very similar to the partial &quot;re-write&quot; done in East Asia (except for werewolves... of course they are the same everywhere. Even though Native American shapechanging myths don't really fit with the legends and myths of Europe, but, then again, the European myths don't really match up very well with the Garou either).<br /> <br /> So... you've got to make choices. If you want the Aztec gods to be renegade vampires and retool what supernaturals you can that are vaguely vampire-like to fill the same roles, you can definitely do so. It's already been done a little bit here and there. (There are game to game issues, as always. If Hutzilopochtli is Shaitan, then it makes it hard for there to be mages in the Aztec priesthood with all of Mage's issues with vampire blood and ghouls and magic, etc.) If you want to keep the mythology intact, you probably have a LOT of work to do and might need to create entire categories of supernatural being that don't exist in the West and probably have to chuck a lot of the &quot;vampires did it&quot;. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:42:19-07:00","id":998841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=998770#post998770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there were no Native American Archmages?</div> </div> </div> </div>I shamefully forgot about them. <br /> Their methods - stemming as they did from petty superstitions - were insufficient against plagues introduced by those whose capabilities stemmed from Reason and Excellence.<br /> <br /> Perhaps their arrogance was their downfall - they didn't think that a scientifically/technocratically induced plague could be so dangerous. And they constantly underestimated the illnesses' ability to spread and spread.<br /> Perhaps they weren't united, especially compared to Order of Reason.<br /> Also, Order of Reason might have received aid from Nephandi. Possibly from Nephandi who presented themselves to the Order as the usual Mages. So Americas got hit by two kinds of Magickal plague-breeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-05-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:43:45-07:00","id":998864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=998841#post998841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Order of Reason might have received aid from Nephandi. Possibly from Nephandi who presented themselves to the Order as the usual Mages. So Americas got hit by two kinds of Magickal plague-breeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's the WoD of M20, then, of course they were helped by the Nephandi. The Nephandi effectively ARE the Technocracy. They're effectively cackling behind every curtain out there. So they have corrupted the Traditions (probably why the European mages turned a blind eye to the whole thing, despite their Dreamspeaker buddies, or, in fact, took advantage of the whole thing to spread into new venues) and they are also probably behind the mages of the Americas not joining together to oppose the invasion (which lead to them get picked off piecemeal and/or not assisting each other in fighting the various methods used in the conquest). <br /> <br /> The Nephandi are an awfully convenient way out of pretty much everthing, like that criminal mouse Savoir Faire, they're EVERYWHERE....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T14:54:10-07:00","id":998893,"title":"","content":"It's good you mentioned Technepandi.<i> Infernalism: Path of Screams</i> notes that &quot;an uncomfortable number of Celestial Masters&quot; serve the Void and those that dwell within. It mentions that Order of Reason &quot;converts&quot; bring eerie stability to the K'llasshaa. Proto-Technepandi might be the ones responsible for decimating the civilizations of Americas. The Order of Reason might have even been prideful enough to think that they can't be seduced by the Nephandi - and thus it was relatively easy to set up so that the majority of those members sent to explore the New World were actually Technepandi and their servants.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=998864#post998864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's the WoD of M20, then, of course they were helped by the Nephandi. The Nephandi effectively ARE the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was already in the first Syndicate Convention Book - you have an Arete 7 Syndic giving superb base of operations to a gang of Fomori led by a Black Spiral, and his Enforcer is a Fomor. Fomori are listed as agents available for the Syndicate.<br /> The <i>Book of Shadows </i>mentions persisting rumors that Progenitors have discussed a merger with Nephandi...as bizarre as it might sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-05-2016, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:12:48-07:00","id":998900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=998814#post998814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, you've said that the all the folklore/mythologies (and oh dear, opening that Pandora's jar is definitely a BIG thing) are intact and true, are you going to insert/overlay/shoehorn in the Eurocentric WoD stable of supernaturals? In an &quot;intact&quot; Pre-Columbian Mesoamerica, why are the gods vampires? In a pre-Cherokee North American Southeast, is Ulunsuti a Nosferatu? (If there even should be an Ulunsuti pre-Cherokee...) Why? She may have liked to stick her long fingernail in the livers of sleeping victims to get yummy treats but there's nothing to indicate that she had any problems with sunlight or need for blood. If you want the mythology intact, you are facing a situation very similar to the partial &quot;re-write&quot; done in East Asia (except for werewolves... of course they are the same everywhere. Even though Native American shapechanging myths don't really fit with the legends and myths of Europe, but, then again, the European myths don't really match up very well with the Garou either).</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why the gods are vampires according to the WoD was because of white writers basically culturally appropriated them and didn't properly approach to those cultures that didn't really belong to them very well which is infact a form of racism and colonialism there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=998814#post998814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... you've got to make choices. If you want the Aztec gods to be renegade vampires and retool what supernaturals you can that are vaguely vampire-like to fill the same roles, you can definitely do so. It's already been done a little bit here and there. (There are game to game issues, as always. If Hutzilopochtli is Shaitan, then it makes it hard for there to be mages in the Aztec priesthood with all of Mage's issues with vampire blood and ghouls and magic, etc.) If you want to keep the mythology intact, you probably have a LOT of work to do and might need to create entire categories of supernatural being that don't exist in the West and probably have to chuck a lot of the &quot;vampires did it&quot;. And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only except I don't want want the Aztec gods to be renegade vampires of course but rather being what they actually are, Deities and of course that's also one of my major criticism I have with some aspects of the WoD's racism there where it's main problem lies as well.<br /> <br /> Thing is, it's quite hypocritical that other Deities are explained off as Vampires or Demons and are treated like the &quot;Source of the Myths&quot; but yet the Christian mythos get special treatment which is pretty problematic since the biggest reason being that it robs the legitimacy of those religions and yet why is the Abrahamic mythos more legit than the others? It doesn't make sense to me even if it did, it's still pretty problematic no matter what since delegitimatizing other Deities other than Yahweh is pretty much textbook justification of colonialism and cultural imperialism which is why it's extremely problematic.<br /> <br /> Thing is, if you make all religions/mythos equally legit, then it pretty much aim's the &quot;All Myths are True&quot; setting that I'm trying to propose here especially in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-05-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:27:23-07:00","id":998908,"title":"","content":"Well, the majority of deities tend to be either personification of natural phenomena or cultural folk heroes. Guan Yu, the Chinese god of war and bean curd, is worshipped in the traditional Chinese religion, Buddhism, and Taoism, and he was a real person (and a mortal man). I would not doubt that 4th and 5th generation Kindred (or Dharma 8 or 9 Kuei-Jin) could be worshipped as deities since mortal people can be worshipped as deities. <br /> <br /> I agree that the Caine myth should be considered that, a myth. Anyone who claims to be Caine is, at best, a dishonest 4th generation Kindred who uses his elder powers to impress younger Kindred. Heck, he could be the inspiration for Yahweh, as a burning bush is not beyond the capabilities of a 4th generation Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 11-05-2016, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:33:54-07:00","id":998911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=998908#post998908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the majority of deities tend to be either personification of natural phenomena or cultural folk heroes. Guan Yu, the Chinese god of war and bean curd, is worshipped in the traditional Chinese religion, Buddhism, and Taoism, and he was a real person (and a mortal man). I would not doubt that 4th and 5th generation Kindred (or Dharma 8 or 9 Kuei-Jin) could be worshipped as deities since mortal people can be worshipped as deities.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Guan_Yu#Worship_of_Guan_Yu\" target=\"_blank\">http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Guan_...hip_of_Guan_Yu</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Worship of Guan Yu</b><br /> <br /> Guan Yu was deified as early as the Sui Dynasty (581-618), and is still popularly <a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Worship_%28Neutral_point_of_View%29\" target=\"_blank\">worshipped</a> today among the Chinese people. He is variedly worshiped as an indigenous <a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/China\" target=\"_blank\">Chinese</a> deity, a <a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Bodhisattva\" target=\"_blank\">bodhisattva</a> in the <a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Buddhism\" target=\"_blank\">Buddhist</a> tradition and as a guardian deity in <a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Taoism\" target=\"_blank\">Taoism</a>.<sup><a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Guan_Yu#cite_note-8\" target=\"_blank\">[9]</a></sup> He is also held in high esteem in <a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Confucianism\" target=\"_blank\">Confucianism</a>. These roles are not necessarily contradictory or even distinguished within the Chinese religious system, which often merges multiple ancient philosophies and religions.<br /> <br /> <b>In the Western world, Guan Yu is sometimes called the <a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Taoism\" target=\"_blank\">Taoist</a> <i>God of War</i>, probably because he is one of the most well-known military general worshiped by the Chinese people. This is a misconception of his role, as, unlike Mars or Tyr, Guan Yu as a god does not necessarily <a href=\"http://religion.wikia.com/wiki/Blessing\" target=\"_blank\">bless</a> those who go to battle but rather people who observe the code of brotherhood and righteousness.</b> </div> </div> </div>Also in Chinese religion/mythos, it's actually quite common that people actually become Gods after they die (like &quot;God of the Kitchen&quot; when they serve the Emperor in the afterlife for example) not just &quot;Primitive screwheads worshiping something that is not&quot; (a rather racist narrative) if you understood Chinese mythology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=998908#post998908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the Caine myth should be considered that, a myth. Anyone who claims to be Caine is, at best, a dishonest 4th generation Kindred who uses his elder powers to impress younger Kindred. Heck, he could be the inspiration for Yahweh, as a burning bush is not beyond the capabilities of a 4th generation Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe separate Vampire from Abrahamic mythos, for example Cain wasn't the first vampire but rather exactly what he is who ends up getting killed by a blind archer later on anyways.<br /> <br /> Of course if there's any Vampire progenitor I would rather have is rather Lilith or someone inspired by her and the whole reason why the Caine myth exists at all is only when Vampire society adopted Patriarchy to shift their original female progenitor to a male one especially when their society got more oppressive over time (when they started using blood bonding, ghouling, etc more and more) and slowly shifted away from their (rather feminist) roots of Lilith till the point that modern vampires slowly forgotten what their original roots were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-05-2016, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T16:18:56-07:00","id":998935,"title":"","content":"While I tend to prefer a group event (either an early attempt by Mages to gain immortality or being created by Gaia to serve as the ultimate weapon), a female progenitor (progenitors) would also be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:16:55-08:00","id":999256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=998900#post998900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason why the gods are vampires according to the WoD was because of white writers basically culturally appropriated them and didn't properly approach to those cultures that didn't really belong to them very well which is infact a form of racism and colonialism there.<br /> <br /> Only except I don't want want the Aztec gods to be renegade vampires of course but rather being what they actually are, Deities and of course that's also one of my major criticism I have with some aspects of the WoD's racism there where it's main problem lies as well.<br /> <br /> Thing is, it's quite hypocritical that other Deities are explained off as Vampires or Demons and are treated like the &quot;Source of the Myths&quot; but yet the Christian mythos get special treatment which is pretty problematic since the biggest reason being that it robs the legitimacy of those religions and yet why is the Abrahamic mythos more legit than the others? It doesn't make sense to me even if it did, it's still pretty problematic no matter what since delegitimatizing other Deities other than Yahweh is pretty much textbook justification of colonialism and cultural imperialism which is why it's extremely problematic.<br /> <br /> Thing is, if you make all religions/mythos equally legit, then it pretty much aim's the &quot;All Myths are True&quot; setting that I'm trying to propose here especially in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the rub. It's going to take A LOT of work to do what you are talking about. Effectively an entire KOE with all the trimmings. Some game-relevant material might just need tweaking... <br /> <br /> A &quot;Hengeyokai&quot; that takes the relevant Garou tribes, Bastet, Nuwisha, etc. with some minor mods to set them up outside the &quot;larger word&quot; of Gaia-botherers in Europe.<br /> <br /> The mages have some, but not much, in place. There should probably some Dreamspeakers who are connected to the world at large (as long as your Pre-Contact setting is after the creation of the Traditions... otherwise, ditch that). It might work to base relevant Fellowship-analogues on era-appropriate culture areas. Or, the easy-peasy way out is to just use the DA Spirit Talkers (which is a personal &quot;ick&quot;, but it would DEFINITELY make things a LOT easier). <br /> <br /> Most of the &quot;vampires did it&quot; probably needs to go. A little bit of vampire would go a long way. Gangrel are pretty plastic and there are definitely some indigenous legends that could fit. Perhaps some Nosferatu? They fled far and wide to get away from the Nictuku, after all. But, all in all, the vampires are going to take a big hit.<br /> <br /> I can't recall all the Native American Changeling materials that are already in play, but they definitely have some kind of basis to work from. From what I do remember, it's somewhere between the Fera and the mages in need for reworking. <br /> <br /> There are definitely going to be categories of supernatural that probably deserve their own entire splat. Or they probably can just be folded in as &quot;spirits&quot; and taken out of consideration as being playable. <br /> <br /> You are definitely going to have pick what you mean by Pre-Columbian. Right before Contact? Pleistocene mammoth hunters? Archaic foragers dealing with the climate change of the Hypsithermal? During the &quot;high mythic age&quot; of the Mississippian Culture in North America, Terminal Classic Maya in Mesoamerica and the Chimu Empire in South America (among many, many others)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:35:10-08:00","id":999263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990992-pre-columbian-wod?p=999256#post999256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are definitely going to have pick what you mean by Pre-Columbian. Right before Contact? Pleistocene mammoth hunters? Archaic foragers dealing with the climate change of the Hypsithermal? During the &quot;high mythic age&quot; of the Mississippian Culture in North America, Terminal Classic Maya in Mesoamerica and the Chimu Empire in South America (among many, many others)</div> </div> </div> </div>What I was originally thinking of taking place around the same time as the Dark Ages gamelines instead it's set in Pre-Columbian America especially those who don't want to play in the European &quot;Dark Medieval&quot; setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:53:34-08:00","id":999443,"title":"","content":"A Dark Ages temporal equivalent for the Western Hemisphere is going to be a lot of major civilizations falling to pieces. <br /> <br /> Which sounds about right as far as equivalencies go....<br /> <br /> But you are going to have do some homework to ID the cultures involved. And they won't be all that similar to modern &quot;Native American&quot; tropes. <br /> <br /> You could make it much simpler by focusing on a specific area and just plunging in. But you won't really have legends or myths for the most part. You'll have archaeology and extrapolation, with some attempts to connect up such things to things known from the Contact Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:12:31-08:00","id":999452,"title":"","content":"For example, the Aztec and Inca Empires did not exist until the early 15th century. Dark Ages takes place in the late 12th century and early 13th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T17:19:26-08:00","id":999497,"title":"","content":"But you have Zapotec, Post-classic Maya, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}